From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 20:58:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: add the MPM interrupt controller

Describe the MSM Power Manager mirror (vMPM) that lives in the APSS
slice of the RPM message RAM, so a system-level power collapse can arm
hardware wakeup pins and notify RPM.

Every value is a verified translation of the downstream msm8998-pm.dtsi
MPM node:

 - the vMPM sits at physical 0x7781b8, i.e. offset 0x1b8 inside
   sram@778000 -- the same slice offset qcm2290 uses;
 - the doorbell is the APCS IPC register 0x17911008 bit 1 downstream;
   mainline's qcom,msm8998-apcs-hmss-global writes BIT(chan) at
   apcs_base + 8 = 0x17911008, so <&apcs_glb 1> is an exact match;
 - the RPM-to-APSS wakeup summary is GIC_SPI 171 edge-rising,
   verbatim from the downstream node;
 - the pin map is the downstream qcom,gic-map with the raw GIC hwirq
   translated to the SPI number (hwirq - 32).  Six of the seven
   downstream entries survive; pin 81 duplicates hwirq 379 (pin 79
   carries it) and is dropped, matching what gic_hwirq_is_mapped()
   would do anyway.  Cross-checked against this file's consumers:
   184 = tsens1 "uplow", 180/347/243 = usb3 "pwr_event"/"qusb2_phy"/
   "ss_phy_irq", 326 = spmi "periph_irq".

Route the SPMI arbiter's summary interrupt through MPM pin 87: the
PMIC PON (power key) and the PMIC RTC alarm both arrive through it, so
it is the wake guarantee for any sleep state deep enough to stop the
GIC.  The pmic-arb requests this line as a chained interrupt, which
suspend_device_irqs() never masks, so the pin's vMPM ENABLE bit -- set
at startup unmask time -- stays armed across every suspend.

No "#power-domain-cells": this firmware only implements PSCI Platform
Coordinated mode, so the MPM is not a genpd provider here; the vMPM
handover runs from the driver's system-suspend path instead.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
index 56e78d29b7ff..f7d48ec56079 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -839,6 +839,23 @@ rpmpd_opp_turbo_plus: opp10 {
 				};
 			};
 		};
+
+		mpm: interrupt-controller {
+			compatible = "qcom,mpm";
+			qcom,rpm-msg-ram = <&apss_mpm>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 171 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+			mboxes = <&apcs_glb 1>;
+			interrupt-controller;
+			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&intc>;
+			qcom,mpm-pin-count = <96>;
+			qcom,mpm-pin-map = <2 184>,  /* tsens1 uplow */
+					   <31 180>, /* usb30 pwr_event */
+					   <52 243>, /* qmp_usb3 lfps_rxterm */
+					   <79 347>, /* qusb2phy dmse/dpse_hv */
+					   <80 352>, /* sp_rmb sp2soc */
+					   <87 326>; /* spmi periph_irq */
+		};
 	};
 
 	smem {
@@ -1397,8 +1414,15 @@ gcc: clock-controller@100000 {
 		};
 
 		rpm_msg_ram: sram@778000 {
-			compatible = "qcom,rpm-msg-ram";
+			compatible = "qcom,rpm-msg-ram", "mmio-sram";
 			reg = <0x00778000 0x7000>;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <1>;
+			ranges = <0 0x00778000 0x7000>;
+
+			apss_mpm: sram@1b8 {
+				reg = <0x1b8 0x48>;
+			};
 		};
 
 		qfprom: qfprom@784000 {
@@ -3068,7 +3092,7 @@ spmi_bus: spmi@800f000 {
 			      <0x0800a000 0x3000>;
 			reg-names = "core", "chnls", "obsrvr", "intr", "cnfg";
 			interrupt-names = "periph_irq";
-			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 326 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupts-extended = <&mpm 87 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			qcom,ee = <0>;
 			qcom,channel = <0>;
 			#address-cells = <2>;
